  "worked_solution": "The major axis is the longest diameter of the ellipse, which is the line segment bounded by the points $(-0.5,-6)$ and $(-0.5,2).$ So, the length of the major axis is $2-(-6)=8.$\n\nThe minor axis is the shortest diameter of the ellipse, which is the line segment bounded by the points $(-2,-2)$ and $(1,-2).$ So, the length of the minor axis is $1-(-2)=3.$",
